From: meta-dogzilla <noreply@qt.io>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] linuxjoystickinput: unref udev_device on the already-attached
 early-continue (fix udev_device leak)

LinuxJoystickInput::probeJoypads() runs on a timer and re-enumerates every
"input" subsystem device. For each device already in m_attached_devices (i.e.
an already-connected joypad, on every poll after the first) it `continue`s past
the udev_device_unref(dev) at the end of the loop body, leaking one udev_device
plus all of its internal property strings per already-attached device per poll.

Confirmed with LeakSanitizer: the top growing leak stack is
udev_device_new_from_syspath <- probeJoypads() <- timerEvent(), climbing
linearly with poll rate. Unref the device before the early continue.

qtgamepad's dev branch is effectively unmaintained; carry locally.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: meta-dogzilla <noreply@qt.io>
---
 src/plugins/joystickinputs/linux/linuxjoystickinput.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/joystickinputs/linux/linuxjoystickinput.cpp b/src/plugins/joystickinputs/linux/linuxjoystickinput.cpp
index 1d8d1b0..5834933 100644
--- a/src/plugins/joystickinputs/linux/linuxjoystickinput.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/joystickinputs/linux/linuxjoystickinput.cpp
@@ -88,8 +88,10 @@ void LinuxJoystickInput::probeJoypads()
             QString devnode_str = devnode;

             // check if exists
-            if (std::find(m_attached_devices.begin(), m_attached_devices.end(), devnode_str) != m_attached_devices.end())
+            if (std::find(m_attached_devices.begin(), m_attached_devices.end(), devnode_str) != m_attached_devices.end()) {
+                udev_device_unref(dev);
                 continue;
+            }

             if (!devnode_str.contains(ignore_str))
                 setupJoypadObject(devnode_str);
